config RTCTRL_MAILBOX
	tristate "Robot real-time DMA mailbox"
	depends on OF && HAS_IOMEM && HAS_DMA && RESET_CONTROLLER && 64BIT
	select MISC_DEVICES
	help
	  Platform driver for a robot control mailbox shared with a RISC-V control
	  endpoint or FPGA. Userspace uses fixed-size, kernel-staged ioctls; only the
	  kernel and endpoint access the coherent-DMA rings. A kernel watchdog forces
	  the hardware enable line low when accepted command submissions stop or a
	  command lease expires. A dedicated reset controller is required to stop
	  endpoint bus mastering if the normal DMA-quiesce handshake fails.

	  The block is not a native RK3588 peripheral. Enable it only when the board
	  device tree describes compatible mailbox hardware or firmware.
